<title>FRANCE: New York remains top airport for Paris imports.</title>
<headline>New York remains top airport for Paris imports.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-09-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Paris airports authority, the Aeroports de Paris (ADP), said New York was the top airport gateway for imports to Charles de Gaulle and Orly airports in the first eight months of 1996.</p>
<p>January-August 1996 Paris-New York air cargo volume totalled 26,434 tonnes, down 3.4 percent on the same period last year, ADP figures showed.</p>
<p>In second place, was Chicago, with 19,277 tonnes, an increase of 13.6 percent on the first eight months of 1995.</p>
<p>Hong Kong was ranked third with 12,106 tonnes flown ex-Paris last month, a fall of 9.7 percent on 1995 levels, ADP said.</p>
<p>The top ten airport gateways for ADP imports between January and August 1996 and the percentage change on the same period in 1995 were as follows:</p>
<p> 1  New York	  26,434 tonnes    (-3.4 pct)</p>
<p> 2  Chicago	   19,277 tonnes   (+13.6)</p>
<p> 3  Hong Kong	 12,106 tonnes    (-9.7)</p>
<p> 4  Los Angeles     11,298 tonnes    (-6.9)</p>
<p> 5  Tokyo	     10,259 tonnes   (-17.8)</p>
<p> 6  Montreal	   9,242 tonnes    (+0.5)</p>
<p> 7  Miami		4,944 tonnes    (-5.0)</p>
<p> 8  Casablanca	 4,267 tonnes   (-10.7)</p>
<p> 9  Dubai		3,650  tonnes   (+2.7)</p>
<p> 10 Johannesburg     3,350  tonnes  (+13.0)</p>
